  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "There are 3 methods to use a dropdowns",
      "text": "1. [details and summary elements](#method-1-details-and-summary)  \n2. [popover API and anchor positioning `new`](#method-2-popover-api-and-anchor-positioning-new)  \n3. [CSS focus](#method-3-css-focus)  ",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Method 1. details and summary",
      "text": "details and summary are native HTML elements that can be used to create dropdowns.  \nDropdown using details and summary opens and closes the content when the summary is clicked. You can also open/close it using JS by adding/removing the `open` attribute",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Method 2. popover API and anchor positioning `new`",
      "text": "Popover API is the new HTML standard for creating dropdowns. It opens the dropdown on a top layer, which means there's no need to z-index management and there's no overflow issue.  \nAnchor positioning is a new CSS standard for positioning elements relative to an anchor.  ",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Method 2. popover API and anchor positioning `new`",
      "text": "> :INFO:\n>\n> `popovertarget` is the unique ID of the popover content.  \n> `anchor-name`/`position-anchor` is the unique name of the anchor.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Method 3. CSS focus",
      "text": "The content gets displayed when the button is focused.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Method 3. CSS focus",
      "text": "> :INFO:\n>\n> Why div?  \n> Safari has a [CSS bug](https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=22261) since 2008 that prevents button elements from being focused, so we use div `tabindex=\"0\"` as a workaround.\n> This approach is accessible with the addition of `role=\"button\"` and functions consistently across all browsers.\n\n> :INFO:\n>\n> This dropdown closes when focus is lost. Avoid placing elements in it that remove focus from dropdown content. For example a `<dialog>` element inside the dropdown.\n\n> :SUCCESS:\n>\n> To close the dropdown after click, you can use something like `onclick=\"document.activeElement.blur()\"`. [Example](https://play.tailwindcss.com/pc8zXb89lM)",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
